 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Knowing the parts helps to use and care for equipment.\nPressure cooker: the pan (body), the lid with a rubber gasket (sealing ring), the safety valve, the weight or pressure regulator on the vent pipe, and the handles.\nBlender: the motor base with speed buttons, the jug (goblet) with measurement marks, the blades at the bottom, the lid and the filler cap.\nVacuum flask: the outer case, a double-walled glass or steel inner container with a vacuum between the walls, silvered (shiny) surfaces, the stopper and the cup.\nMicrowave oven: the door with a window and safety lock, the turntable (glass plate), the control panel and timer.\nMixer: the motor, speed control, the beaters (whisks) and the bowl.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "t": "the rubber gasket of a pressure cooker"
  },
  "problem": "What is the job of {t}?",
  "steps": [
   "It fits round the edge of the lid.",
   "It seals the lid so steam cannot escape and the pressure can build up."
  ],
  "answer": "It seals the lid to keep the steam and pressure in.",
  "checks": []
 },
